<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Darius I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 522–486 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Darius the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Darius I, also known as Darius the Great, was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> (r. 522–486 BCE). He reorganised the empire into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapies</a> with regular tribute, introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daric">daric</a> coinage, developed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-road">Royal Road</a> and built at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persepolis">Persepolis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>. His reign marked the administrative consolidation of the empire, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> note the continued use of Elamite administrative traditions under his rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/darius-i.jpg" alt="Darius I" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rumlu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Darius_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
